  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Janus’s self-storage and industrial door markets provide stable but cyclical demand. Recent results show mixed trends: Q4 margin gains were offset by a soft outlook, while Q1 margin pressure emerged alongside modest revenue growth. Product innovation is a bright spot, but macro uncertainty and cautious end-markets weigh on activity. The business is viewed as resilient, with upside if conditions stabilize.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Management has strengthened the balance sheet since IPO, though debt remains elevated. The recent EPS miss and guidance cut have dented credibility, yet product innovation signals a focus on competitiveness. The stock’s depressed valuation reflects these execution concerns, but a deleveraging and organic growth strategy could catalyze a re-rating if macro headwinds ease.",
